ment–determination–process–resources, each dimension has an impor­
tant impact on the effect of water pollution collaborative governance. 
However, achieving efficient governance depends not only on the 
driving force of a single condition but also on the comprehensive effect 
of multiple conditions (Kelli et al., 2013). Despite the defects of one 
governance condition, efficient water pollution collaborative gover­
nance can still be achieved through the synergistic action of multiple 
conditions. This means that research on the mechanism of water 
pollution collaborative governance cannot ignore the synergistic and 
matching effects among various conditions. This research introduces 
this framework into the QCA model to explore the configuration effects 
among the six conditions under four key dimensions: regional gover­
nance environment, regional governance determination, regional 
governance process, and regional governance resources. The logical 
relationship is shown in Fig. 1. 
4. Research design 
4.1. Research method 
Most existing literature uses traditional regression methods, game 
theory, and QCA methods to study collaborative governance issues (Rao 
and Zhao, 2022; Wang and Wang, 2023; Xu and Wu, 2020). Through 
comparison, it was found that the QCA method is used to analyze 
whether a certain condition is necessary for the generation of a result, 
and focuses on the combination configuration of conditions. The ad­
vantages of this method are reflected in three main aspects: First, 
compared with traditional regression analysis, the QCA method pro­
vides a new perspective from which to analyze the complex causal 
relationship of multiple factors. Traditional regression analysis often 
focuses on the influence of a single variable on the results. QCA em­
phasizes the interaction and combination effect of multiple variables 
(Du and Jia, 2017). This approach enables an understanding of the 
causal logic underlying complex management phenomena from a ho­
listic and systematic perspective rather than simply ascribing these 
phenomena to individual factors. Second, compared with game theory, 
QCA provides researchers with a deeper, more comprehensive under­
standing through a combination of qualitative and quantitative analysis. 
Game theory often requires researchers to make assumptions about 
participants’ preferences, strategies, and payments, and accurate 
Fig. 1. Collaborative governance mechanism of the Yangtze River Basin in China.  
F. Zhao et al.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
Journal of Environmental Management 360 (2024) 121217
5
information is needed to support the construction of the model. The QCA 
method is more flexible and enables qualitative comparison of the fuzzy 
relationships between multiple variables. The qualitative analysis of the 
QCA method can capture nonlinear and asymmetric relationships that 
are difficult to quantify using traditional statistical methods, while 
quantitative analysis provides rigorous data support and verification 
(Niu et al., 2020). This comprehensive analysis strategy enables re­
searchers to more accurately understand how various factors in man­
agement practice interweave to influence the final outcome. Third, from 
the perspective of the actual development of transboundary collabora­
tive governance, water pollution collaborative governance in the 
Yangtze River Basin may imply an “equivalent” causal chain, with the 
same result under the guidance of multiple paths. The QCA method has 
significant advantages in exploring the causal logic behind complex 
management phenomena. The QCA method interprets the results of the 
explained variables by identifying different antecedent condition con­
figurations, and is more suitable for exploring the action path and 
optimization 
of 
transboundary 
water 
pollution 
collaborative 
governance. 
However, the traditional QCA is limited in theory and tools, mostly 
stuck in cross-section data, and it is difficult to explore the temporal 
longitudinal configuration effect. Since 2015, basin collaborative 
governance has stepped into a rapid development channel, which is a 
continuous event occurring on the time axis. The section configuration 
alone is not enough to explain the interaction between causality and 
time. 
Based on the above considerations, this study refers to the study of 
Zhang (2023) and adopts the dynamic QCA method. It also refers to the 
relevant theories and methods proposed by Garcia-Castro and Ari˜no 
(2016), uses R language software to break the barrier between panel 
data and QCA, and explores the configuration relationship under the 
time effect. 
Before applying the dynamic QCA method, a clear theoretical 
framework was constructed to clarify the core questions and key vari­
ables of the study to ensure clear guidance for the analysis process. In 
addition, in the identification of antecedent conditions, this study fully 
considers the actual conditions to ensure the effectiveness and reliability 
of the dynamic QCA method in practical applications. 
4.2. Research objects and data sources 
The main stream of the Yangtze River spans 11 provinces and mu­
nicipalities in China. Thus, it is a representative case to explore the 
collaborative control of transboundary water pollution in the Yangtze 
River basin. In light of data availability, this study deleted 53 trans­
boundary sections, such as Chenqian, and selected for inclusion 171 
transboundary sections, such as Baiyangxi, in the main stream of the 
Yangtze River. 
The Decision of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of 
China on Several Major Issues Concerning Comprehensively Deepening 
Reform in 2014 mentioned that a new model of “transboundary gover­
nance” with Chinese characteristics should be built by drawing on the 
Western concept of “governance” and combining traditional Chinese 
culture and basic national conditions. The Environmental Protection 
Law of the People’s Republic of China came into effect on January 1, 
2015, so the research period covered in this study spans from 2015 to 
2021. 
The 171 sections were matched with the data of 57 cities to construct 
