level of control (high/low) attributed to an actor group. This 
is an important indicator, as it suggests who is actually in 
charge of policy processes. The results presented in Table 7 
suggest that relatively little control is assigned to non-state 
actors, either domestic or international. By contrast, con-
trol is overwhelmingly assigned to international state actors 
