and Antonsich 2009; Mackelworth 2012).
But even when high-ranking politicians are involved, there are a signiﬁcant num-
ber of cases where environmental cooperation had little to no impact on the sym-
bolic relations between states. These include Costa Rica-Nicaragua (Barquet 2015),
the Sava River Basin (Colakhodži et al. 2014), South Africa-Zimbabwe-Mozambique
(van Amerom and Büscher 2005), and Turkey-Syria (Scheumann and Shamaly
2016). Also, disaster-related cooperation, for instance between Greece and Turkey
after the 1999 Izmir earthquake (Akcinaroglu et al. 2011), has at best a short-term
