problems 
Collaborative governance is effective to solve interdependent natural 
resource management problems when stakeholders do not already 
participate in other collaborative venues and/or they have a weak 
social capital. 
Collaboration with organizations active in other sectors is preferred 
when natural resource managers are constrained to act within one 
