Only those events were included where the source of tension referred to ‘‘food, water, or subsistence.” The source could be mentioned as either a ﬁrst, second, or third issue of
tension. Social disturbances are then overlaid with water risk categories in upstream protected land. Social disturbance data is based on SCAD (Salehyan et al., 2012) and
water risk data comes from the World Resource Institute (Gassert et al., 2014).
